messages:
jean: Quick heads-up  opened a docs PR to update Halcyon9B model card. Main items: clarify supported sequence lengths per variant, add small-batch vs large-batch bench rows, fix an incorrect link to the runtime compat page, and include a short Rust SDK snippet for streaming embeddings with shard hints. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4976 :sparkles:

owen: thanks. can you call out which variant is safe for embedding sharding? last time the card said all variants were shardable but one of the quant builds had issues.

jean: good catch. I'll explicitly list shardable variants (halcyon9b-fp16, halcyon9b-int8-shardable) and mark halcyon9b-int8-compact as non-shardable with a short rationale.

mika: for the bench table please show columns: variant, GPU, batch_size, seq_len, tokens/s. customers keep asking for GPU in the table. also add a note about pinning sequence length for peak-throughput runs.

jean: done. added GPU column and a footnote: "peak runs pinned seqlen using pinned-seqlen flag". splitting bench into 3 rows per variant for clarity.

owen: also replace the old runtime link with https://docs.redwood.ai/runtime/compatibility#precision-and-kv-cache and remove the stale reference to runtime v1.8.

jean: updated link and removed the stale paragraph. docs-bot, run the markdown linter when ready.

docs-bot: lint check  models/halcyon9b.md: headings OK, but found one broken link (line 94) and one long line warning (line 121).

jean: fixing those now. adding the Rust SDK snippet as requested (keeps an example for teams using Rust):

```rust
use redwood_rs::Client;
#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
  let client = Client::new(std::env::var("REDWOOD_KEY")?);
  let mut stream = client.embeddings_stream("halcyon9b", "let x = 42;", Some("code:high"), None).await?;
  while let Some(chunk) = stream.next().await {
    let emb = chunk?.embedding;
    println!("{}", &emb[..8].iter().map(|v| v.to_string()).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(", "));
  }
  Ok(())
}
```

qa-sam: please add the eval checklist before merging: reproduce bench on A100-80GB and A100-40GB, run tokenization diff on 100 prompts, run idempotency test for embedding shard merges. I'll queue tests after PR lands (ETA ~5h).

jean: will add checklist and tag reviewers @owen @mika @qa-sam. target merge before the next catalog publish. :calendar:
